# mbsync (isync) — Gmail → local Maildir mirror. Phase 1 of #46 (archive-only).
# Password lives in a 600 file (never in git/chezmoi); paste it from Proton Pass.

IMAPAccount gmail
Host imap.gmail.com
User im.bitter.smiles@gmail.com
PassCmd "cat ~/.config/mbsync/gmail.pass"
TLSType IMAPS
CertificateFile /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt

IMAPStore gmail-remote
Account gmail

MaildirStore gmail-local
Path ~/mail/gmail/
Inbox ~/mail/gmail/Inbox
SubFolders Verbatim

Channel gmail
Far :gmail-remote:
Near :gmail-local:
# Skip [Gmail]/All Mail — it holds a *copy* of every message, so pulling it
# doubles the archive. Also skip the virtual Important/Starred labels.
#
# Three labels were retired on Gmail around 2026-10-28 and their mail moved into other labels:
# Personal/Tax, Works/DSVN and Works/FSOFT. Their local Maildirs are the only remaining copy of the
# *labels*, but not of the mail — sampled Message-IDs from all three are present in All Mail, so the
# messages still exist server-side under their new labels (which `*` picks up). Gmail answers SELECT
# with `[NONEXISTENT]` for them, which made every run fail with "far side box ... cannot be opened
# anymore" (exit 1, four runs). Excluded rather than deleted: Expunge None means the 62 local
# messages stay readable as an archive, and nothing is ever removed server-side.
Patterns * !"[Gmail]/All Mail" !"[Gmail]/Important" !"[Gmail]/Starred" !"Personal/Tax" !"Works/DSVN" !"Works/FSOFT"
Create Near
Expunge None          # archive-only: never delete anything server-side
SyncState *
